{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310587,"nonce":"ys3lH4oY/xH3ZD1aauoCEhMUhY4=","title":"FIXED 862f51d0 by guarding the READER — haxe_std_string_ptr validates the slot before dereferencing; every attempt to change the PRODUCER ...","message":"**FIXED 2026-09-11 in 862f51d0 — BY GUARDING THE READER, NOT THE PRODUCER.**\n`haxe_std_string_ptr` (runtime/src/type_system.rs) checked only `is_null()` and\nthen read the slot as a `DynamicValue`. It now goes through `dynamic_box_at`\n(the shared address gate added in c863b177) and stringifies a NON-BOX as the\ninteger it is. Fixture: `haxe-conformance/regressions/DynamicElements.hx`\ncovers index / iteration / concat / join / Std.string / arithmetic / Map.get\n— the corpus covers NONE of them.\n\nMEASURED: conformance 502 -\u003e 502, ZERO rows changed status except Issue3389\nCRASH -\u003e WRONG_ANSWER (stable 5/5, an improvement). Issue10752 WRONG_ANSWER -\u003e\nCRASH is BISTABLE ON ONE BINARY (crash 3/5, wrong 2/5) — not a regression, and\nit never passes either way. Haxe suite 207/0/1 unchanged.\n\n**HOW IT WAS FOUND — THE CENSUS ANSWERED BY SILENCE.** A temporary\n`RAYZOR_DYNAMIC_CENSUS=1` instrument on `dynamic_box_at` (`#[track_caller]` +\ndedup by call site) printed NOTHING before the crash. That was the finding: the\ncrashing readers never consult the gate AT ALL. The ~8 address heuristics were\nnever the issue on these paths — the issue was ONE reader with NO check.\nInstrument reverted after it paid out (hot-path `#[track_caller]`); re-add in\nfive minutes if needed.\n\n**STILL OPEN, SAME AMBIGUITY, OTHER DIRECTION:** a RAW value that IS aligned\nand \u003e=0x1000 is still read as a box — `Issue3389` prints\n`\u003cunknown type 4063187296\u003e`. Only a self-describing representation fixes that;\nsee [[project_dynamic_primitive_representation_redesign]].\n\n**ORIGINAL REPRO** (`/tmp/probe/U5.hx`):\n```haxe\nvar d:Array\u003cDynamic\u003e = [];\nd.push(1); d.push(2);\nd[0];           // 1 -- correct\nd.join(\",\");    // SIGSEGV, fault=0x1\n```\nAlso crashes when the Dynamic array is filled from a custom iterator\n(`/tmp/probe/U3.hx`, `U6.hx`) — `for (v in new Countdown(3)) a.push(v)` with\n`var a = []`, fault = the first value.\n\n**MECHANISM.** `join` routes through `haxe_array_join_typed` with the element\nTAG (mir/expr/call/array.rs). A Dynamic element is tag 6, and\n`haxe_value_to_string_by_tag` (runtime/src/haxe_sys.rs:599) sends tag 6 to\n`haxe_std_string_ptr(value as *mut u8)` — so a raw `1` is dereferenced as an\naddress. The element is stored RAW: `d[0]` reads it back raw and prints 1.\n\n**ATTEMPT REVERTED (2026-09-11).** Boxing primitives at the push site\n(`box_primitive_as_dynamic` + `haxe_array_push_i64`, guarded to an Array whose\nelement type resolves to Dynamic) FIXED `join=1,2` but BROKE the read:\n`d[0]` then printed the box ADDRESS (43864987184), because the element read\nhas no matching unbox. It also did NOT fix U3/U6, whose element type or value\ntype is not seen as Dynamic/primitive at that site.\n\n**TAG-DURING-UNBOX WAS TRIED AND MEASURED (2026-09-11) — BOTH HALVES FAIL,\nSEPARATELY AND TOGETHER.** The box is self-describing, so a reader can dispatch\non `DynamicValue.type_id` instead of a static type. Implemented as: (a) push\nBOXES a primitive or String into a Dynamic array (guarding on the lowered\nREGISTER type, not the static type — a value from an iterator arrives erased);\n(b) `convert_to_string_with_hint` (mir/types.rs) gains a `Dynamic` arm calling\n`haxe_std_string_ptr`, which reads the tag.\n\nRESULTS, all measured:\n- (a)+(b): the probes it targets all pass — `U5 elem=1 join=1,2`, `U3\n  join=3,2,1`, `U6 dyn-join=2,1`, `U2 join=x,y`. But **conformance 502 -\u003e 500**\n  (LOST Issue3512 `1882054528 != 1`, Issue6674 `1 != 37897980176`) and the S1\n  and M1 probe batteries CRASH. Readers that consume a Dynamic element RAW are\n  widespread; boxing at one producer breaks all of them.\n- (b) alone: WORSE — S1, M1 and even U5 crash, because without boxing a\n  Dynamic is often a raw value and `haxe_std_string_ptr` dereferences it.\n- Still unfixed either way: a String arriving from an ARRAY ITERATOR\n  (`for (s in bag) b.push(s)`, C1's `iterator-method`) is erased at the push\n  site, so even the register-type guard misses it.\n\n**CONCLUSION: the representation cannot be changed one site at a time.** Find\nevery reader of a Dynamic element (index, iteration, concat, join, Std.string,\narithmetic) and convert them together, or leave elements raw and make the\ntag-6 stringify tolerant of a small non-pointer.\n\n**THIS IS THE SAME TWO-REPRESENTATION TRAP as\n[[bugs_parseint_null_sentinel_never_translated]]:** boxing a value only works\nonce EVERY reader unboxes. Either do both sides together (push boxes, index\nand iteration unbox) and measure, or leave it raw and make the tag-6\nstringify path tolerant of a small non-pointer — the runtime already uses an\n`addr \u003e= 0x1000` heuristic in `dynamic_value_if_boxed` and\n`haxe_unbox_scalar_or_addr`.\n\nNo corpus row is known to depend on this; found by probing\n([[feedback_probe_ordinary_semantics_finds_real_bugs]]).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_dynamic_array_elements_stored_raw` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}